1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,646
Imagine a convincing investment offer arriving in your family chat.

2
00:00:05,031 --> 00:00:09,004
Urgent wording and unfamiliar financial terms make it hard to judge.

3
00:00:09,137 --> 00:00:12,779
For first-time investors, the challenge is understanding the request

4
00:00:12,779 --> 00:00:14,983
before money or personal information changes hands.

5
00:00:16,947 --> 00:00:18,519
Now, this is Sajag.

6
00:00:18,673 --> 00:00:20,814
Sajag connects checking with learning.

7
00:00:21,452 --> 00:00:26,140
Bring a message, understand the quoted warning, then explore the lessons behind it.

8
00:00:26,231 --> 00:00:29,641
Our web and Android prototype combines a private offline check

9
00:00:29,641 --> 00:00:31,094
with an optional AI review.

10
00:00:31,094 --> 00:00:33,108
No investment advice.

11
00:00:34,062 --> 00:00:36,098
So, look at the quoted words on screen.

12
00:00:36,462 --> 00:00:40,603
They explain what triggered the warnings, with relevant official guidance and context.

13
00:00:41,493 --> 00:00:43,340
Sharing and saving remain separate choices.

14
00:00:43,767 --> 00:00:47,550
Lessons and fictional simulations turn a warning into understanding.

15
00:00:47,788 --> 00:00:51,276
Android Back returns sections Home after closing overlays.

16
00:00:51,683 --> 00:00:56,055
Now that we have seen what the warning tells us and why these features matter,

17
00:00:57,282 --> 00:00:59,108
let's put them to a test.

18
00:00:59,409 --> 00:01:02,882
We'll move from the explanation to a few actual checks

19
00:01:02,882 --> 00:01:05,592
to see how the system responds to different types of messages.

20
00:01:06,166 --> 00:01:09,949
We'll start with a fictional parcel message asking for ₹49 to release a delivery.

21
00:01:10,314 --> 00:01:12,840
We'll run it locally, give permission for AI review,

22
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:14,939
and then see what the result looks like.

23
00:01:15,071 --> 00:01:18,160
Next, we'll look at a routine insurance premium notice.

24
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:23,254
The offline check raises a pattern warning, and the AI review label

25
00:01:23,534 --> 00:01:29,254
shows why the warning was withdrawn while keeping the result visible as context.

26
00:01:29,745 --> 00:01:33,907
These are genuine website checks using fictional messages,

27
00:01:34,587 --> 00:01:37,296
to demonstrate how the system behaves

28
00:01:39,134 --> 00:01:42,412
without making any claim about real-world accuracy.

29
00:01:43,176 --> 00:01:43,822
AI can still be wrong.

30
00:01:44,502 --> 00:01:48,517
Now look at the language screens: English, Hindi and Bengali are interface choices.

31
00:01:48,881 --> 00:01:55,070
Messages can also use Hinglish and Banglish. That gives 5 tested language forms,

32
00:01:55,070 --> 00:01:58,664
including Romanised Hindi and Bengali.

33
00:01:58,881 --> 00:02:02,516
Bengali remains beta, awaiting native-speaker review.

34
00:02:02,923 --> 00:02:08,579
Look at the counts from the test: 150 synthetic messages,

35
00:02:08,796 --> 00:02:12,417
75 risky and 75 harmless, across 5 language forms.

36
00:02:12,417 --> 00:02:16,432
Offline got 124 correct, which is 82.7%.

37
00:02:16,754 --> 00:02:23,631
With AI, that makes 149 correct, which is 99.3%: a very good accuracy.

38
00:02:24,164 --> 00:02:29,547
Risky messages flagged rose from 57 to 74 out of 75.

39
00:02:29,848 --> 00:02:33,926
Harmless false alarms fell from 8 to 0 out of 75.

40
00:02:34,185 --> 00:02:39,020
AI completed 145 reviews; 5 used offline fallback.

41
00:02:39,385 --> 00:02:41,989
These results are not real-world guarantees,

42
00:02:42,121 --> 00:02:46,094
but yes, these are the testing results of our product.

43
00:02:46,711 --> 00:02:48,810
Follow the two layers on the screen.

44
00:02:49,216 --> 00:02:52,689
Local rules and a small pattern model check wording on the device

45
00:02:52,689 --> 00:02:54,094
without sending any message.

46
00:02:54,226 --> 00:02:57,742
With permission, RAG retrieves relevant SEBI, RBI and government guidance

47
00:02:57,742 --> 00:02:59,272
for Gemini, our AI model.

48
00:02:59,552 --> 00:03:03,483
New AI warnings need matching quoted words and official guidance.

49
00:03:03,889 --> 00:03:06,472
A second pass confirms or withdraws warnings.

50
00:03:06,878 --> 00:03:08,198
Strong results cannot be withdrawn.

51
00:03:08,815 --> 00:03:11,756
Offline provides access; AI adds context.

52
00:03:12,141 --> 00:03:17,236
Next, look at 15 lessons: 7 money concepts and 8 scam lessons.

53
00:03:17,236 --> 00:03:23,251
4 fictional chat stories reveal pressure tactics through your choices.

54
00:03:23,825 --> 00:03:27,966
A small task-job reward can lead to deposit demands.

55
00:03:28,330 --> 00:03:34,008
In the money simulator, a 20% loss needs a 25% rise to recover.

56
00:03:34,267 --> 00:03:36,067
This is arithmetic, not a forecast.

57
00:03:36,730 --> 00:03:38,513
Users create and verify their account once,

58
00:03:38,856 --> 00:03:41,187
and returning users sign in securely with their password.

59
00:03:41,530 --> 00:03:45,804
Before every AI check, users can see what information will be shared

60
00:03:45,804 --> 00:03:47,629
and give explicit permission.

61
00:03:48,098 --> 00:03:53,397
Sensitive content is masked before it leaves the device,

62
00:03:53,614 --> 00:03:57,782
and users remain in control of what they choose to save.

63
00:03:57,782 --> 00:04:03,397
Core features continue to work offline, while AI review is used only by user choice.

64
00:04:04,014 --> 00:04:07,592
AI submissions may be subject to the provider's data policies,

65
00:04:07,592 --> 00:04:10,470
and locally saved notebook data is not encrypted.

66
00:04:11,024 --> 00:04:15,817
Sajag brings warning, explanation and practice together into a learning journey,

67
00:04:15,908 --> 00:04:20,981
helping people not just identify a risky message, but understand why it is risky

68
00:04:20,981 --> 00:04:23,817
and make a safer decision next time.

69
00:04:24,044 --> 00:04:27,954
This is Sajag by Team FirstBest: Anshuman Biswal and me, Masud Ali.

70
00:04:28,781 --> 00:04:29,996
Understand before you act.
